# Security Rules

## Content Security Policy
- `script-src` has no `unsafe-inline` or `unsafe-eval`
- All inline `<script>` tags **must** include `nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}"`
- Never add `unsafe-inline` or `unsafe-eval` to the CSP header in `app.py`

## Secrets & Credentials
- Never hard-code API keys, DB passwords, or tokens
- All secrets come from environment variables (see `.env.example`)
- The following are safe to commit (non-secret IDs): Supabase project ref, Google OAuth Client ID, Vercel project/team IDs

## Authentication
- Admin routes: `_admin_check()` — requires `ADMIN_TOKEN` via `?token=` or `X-Admin-Token` header
- User routes: Flask session (`session["user_id"]`)
- Google OAuth: PKCE flow via Supabase JS — do not change the redirect flow without reading AGENTS.md

## Database
- Production: Supabase PostgreSQL via Transaction pooler (port **6543**)
- Never use SQLite in production (Vercel `/tmp` is ephemeral)
- Always use `sslmode=require` in DB connection strings
